The Ray-sweeping algorithm is an improvement over the Warm-up Algorithm because it has a linear time complexity, making it more efficient than its predecessor. The Parenting process of this algorithm involves three main steps: enumerating A\ud835\udc5b\n2 (enumeration), computing medians and identifying high-skew projections in constant time, and updating the skew values efficiently by sweeping a ray counterclockwise from the x-axis to the y-axis. This approach is based on our earlier observation that while moving between two neighboring median regions, the set of dual lines above/below the median changes by only one element . 

The Ray-sweeping algorithm maintains some aggregates while sweeping over A\ud835b\n2, which enables updating the skew values in constant time. The pseudo-code for this approach is provided in Algorithm 1. A visualization of this algorithm on a toy example is provided in Figure 3.

